PATCH 520: the last thirteen arg-less `lcall [0x6b4]` cockpit handlers.

Completes the batch started by patches 517/518/519.  Every one had its ENTIRE body emitted by Ghidra as
`(*(code *)fist_icall_far((uint32_t)(DAT_1000_c6b4)))(); return;`.  DAT_2000_2d34 is the PLAYER's NEAR
OFFSET (patch 300); BX is the display-list element's near offset, which both the 2057 and 209e walks
publish to DGROUP:0x3e08, and BP the walk base (g_fist_paintbp, patch 142).

  7597   the odd one out: `movzbw ax,[0x8d5f] ; add ax,0x1460 ; mov bx,0x8dc4` -- the glyph index comes
         from byte[DGROUP:0x8d5f], not the player, and BX is FIXED (DI is loaded and then unused).
  7fff   `mov ax,[di+0x5d] ; mov bx,0x1a ; mul bx ; mov bx,dx ; and bx,0x1e ; mov ax,[bx-0x6fec]`
         -- a 16x16 multiply whose HIGH half indexes word[DGROUP:0x9014 + ix].
  8ba1   `mov bl,[di+0x5f] ; shr bl,1 x3 ; and bx,0x1e ; mov gs,[0x70] ; mov ax,gs:[bx+0x2740]`
  906d   the same with `shr bl,3` and table gs:0x2b10
  9ab5   `mov bl,[di+0x63] ; and bx,0xf ; shl bx,1 ; mov gs,[0x70] ; mov ax,gs:[bx+0x290c]`
         -- these three go through the `mov gs,[0x70]` STRING SEGMENT, the same base patch 510 had to
         restore in 8463 and which Ghidra drops every time.
  8668   `mov bl,[di+0x63] ; and bx,0xf ; shl bx,1 ; mov ax,[bx-0x6f40]`   (DGROUP:0x90c0)
  8708   the same, table DGROUP:0x91d0, then `add ax,0x9d0`
  8725   byte[di+0x64], table DGROUP:0x91d0, then `add ax,0x9f0`
  8d88, 6e3d, 97da   FUN_0000_80eb's shape (patch 504): a three-way base chosen by byte[bp+[bx+2]+1],
         then +8 if it matches byte[di+0x86] else + byte[di+0x3f].  Bases 0x768/0x778/0x788,
         0x14c0/0x14d0/0x14e0 and 0xa80/0xa90/0xaa0.
  7100   `mov bl,[bp+si+1] ; movzbw ax,bl ; shl ax,4 ; add ax,0x1510`, then +8 if bl == byte[di+0x90]
         else + byte[di+0x3f]
  96bb   `mov bl,[bp+si+1] ; mov ax,[bx-0x6dc6]` (DGROUP:0x923a, byte-indexed -- the ids are pre-scaled),
         then +8 if bl == byte[di+0x91] else + byte[di+0x3f]

With this the 48-handler set is closed: 5 in 517, 11 in 518, 24 in 519, 13 here (7597 and the rest).
--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -20173,7 +20173,13 @@
 void __allregs FUN_0000_7597(void)
 
 {
-  (*(code *)fist_icall_far((uint32_t)(DAT_1000_c6b4)))();
+  /* PATCH 520: asm 0x7597-0x75aa `mov di,[0x6d34] ; movzbw ax,[0x8d5f] ; add ax,0x1460 ;
+   * mov bx,0x8dc4 ; lcall [0x6b4]`.  Unlike its neighbours this one takes the glyph index from
+   * byte[DGROUP:0x8d5f] and uses a FIXED bx=0x8dc4 -- it does NOT read the display-list element (DI is
+   * loaded and then unused).  Ghidra emitted the whole body as a bare arg-less `lcall [0x6b4]`. */
+  unsigned char *dg = (unsigned char *)g_mem + 0x1c000;
+  unsigned short ax = (unsigned short)(dg[0x8d5f] + 0x1460);
+  (*(code *)fist_icall_far((uint32_t)(DAT_1000_c6b4)))(ax,0x8dc4);
   return;
 }
 
